for early cancer detection, starting with colon cancer.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/475ac666b51753e4e86ee7902ee204cb","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-10-05T14:00:13.000Z"},{"id":"Fzu5y_2cw","title":"Did We Overeat on Software?","url":"https://future.com/did-we-overeat-on-software/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/did-we-overeat-on-software--fzu5y-2cw","summary":"The average number of apps deployed per Okta customer has risen 22% over the past 4 years. Up to 25% of SaaS apps and licenses go unused for many companies. Companies often think that centralization is the answer but, in this case, it\u2019s not. There are simply too many apps to contend with.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/9cde2ef2cb1e467ce61991175591c381","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-09-27T14:00:05.000Z"},{"id":"uvDO2FbsC","title":"Our Cities Have an API Problem. Startups Can Fix It.","url":"https://future.com/cities-broken-api/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/our-cities-have-an-api-problem-startups-can-fix-it--uvdo2fbsc","summary":"Frida Ghitis: America's cities have an API problem: How do American cities measure up as technology? She says the core API of the city is its land use policy, which makes it hard to build. She says if you want to build in U.S. cities, you must integrate with their Land Use policy.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/6e7d624ecf13c30621f99b99b4c19644","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-09-13T15:00:28.000Z"},{"id":"rTYnGQwsp","title":"Research Twice, Build Once: How to Know Your Users as You Grow","url":"https://future.com/user-research-as-you-grow/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/research-twice-build-once-how-to-know-your-users-as-you-grow-rtyngqwsp","summary":"User research is the unsung hero of determining a product\u2019s viability and the secret ingredient to its success. Early stage teams may be aware of user research, but might not know where to start. Companies already starting to scale up may start to wonder about best practices for integrating research into a growing organization.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/d577fafc1892b12bca4751f5d8685810","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-09-01T14:00:09.000Z"},{"id":"kKa3fueHs","title":"Grow or Die: A Framework for Turning Your Company Around Fast","url":"https://future.com/grow-or-die-supergoals/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/grow-or-die-a-framework-for-turning-your-company-around-fast-kka3fuehs","summary":"A Framework for Turning Your Company Around Fast is a framework that I've come to call SuperGoals. It's a high stakes, focusing goal for a team, an open-ended method of achievement, and a single measure of success that everyone can understand. The framework is designed to encourage an \u2018all hands on deck\u2019","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/86487a57370016153bc1a796d98fc458","num_upvotes":15,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-08-31T18:22:46.000Z"},{"id":"W-IjO_MwL","title":"What Synthetic Embryos Can and Can\u2019t Do, Now and in the Future","url":"https://future.com/what-synthetic-embryos-can-do/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/what-synthetic-embryos-can-and-can-t-do-now-and-in-the-future-w-ijo-mwl","summary":"Magdalena Zernicka-Goetz is the Bren Professor of Biology and Biological Engineering at the California Institute of Technology and a Professor of Stem Cell Biology and Development at the University of Cambridge. She explains how these \u2018synthetic\u2019 embryos are built and the limits of their similarity to natural embryos grown from fertil.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/920ad5a941162fc0830d24f1650201fd","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-08-30T14:40:32.000Z"},{"id":"KOx_3CuR3","title":"Jason Fried on Why He Doesn\u2019t Do Planning or Politics at Work","url":"https://future.com/jason-fried-basecamp-hey-interview/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/jason-fried-on-why-he-doesn-t-do-planning-or-politics-at-work-kox-3cur3","summary":"Jason Fried is a 37-year-old founder of Basecamp and HEY. Fried has a reputation as a tech industry contrarian over the past two decades. Fried: Why limit teams to just two people? That's enough, that\u2019s enough. We don\u2019t have project managers. Every additional person beyond that, I think things get exponentially more complicated.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f9154c1b3e81ac2b51f83bfb7405673f","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-08-29T15:00:53.000Z"},{"id":"7xmUVp4GN","title":"Thinking Through CC0 and IP for NFT Communities","url":"https://future.com/thinking-through-cc0-and-ip-for-nfts/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/thinking-through-cc0-and-ip-for-nft-communities-7xmuvp4gn","summary":"NFTs are a web3 innovation, but the intellectual property frameworks surrounding them have been borrowed from a web2 world. They can stick with the traditional standard copyright, in which the issuer owns all the IP and buyers just have the rights for personal use. This centralizes creative control You are essentially creating, buying and selling a bundle of IP rights.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/5b82aae39d36b0dd4e1e0a1d5eab7085","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-08-26T15:00:11.000Z"},{"id":"gtfC4lbhL","title":"The Insider\u2019s Guide to Data Rooms: What to Know Before You Raise","url":"https://future.com/insiders-guide-to-data-rooms-fundraising/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-insider-s-guide-to-data-rooms-what-to-know-before-you-raise-gtfc4lbhl","summary":"Data rooms are a key part of the preparation for other liquidity events like IPOs or SPACs. Here we focus on the importance of data rooms when raising venture capital. Here are five things that we often see in data rooms but wouldn't recommend including, unless an investor specifically asks for them: 1. Org chart and/or team bios.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/583b3790eaeb7c6bc7905e459c5ebc54","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-08-25T14:10:10.000Z"},{"id":"BHW9YyPmr","title":"Remote Startups Will Win the War for Top Talent","url":"https://future.com/remote-startups-hire-top-talent/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/remote-startups-will-win-the-war-for-top-talent-bhw9yypmr","summary":"Between 2008 and 2018, remote work exploded 400 percent, resulting in almost 4 million remote workers in the US. By 2030, 50 to 80 million of the world\u2019s 255 million desk jobs will be performed remotely a majority of the time. In the same way e-commerce has decimated many physical stores, virtual companies will crush office-based companies.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/6e40ff7133c482aabfafa1f0e5537318","num_upvotes":23,"num_comments":8,"created_at":"2022-08-23T14:00:40.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["smashing","circle","theodo","halodoc","habr"],"opposite_handles":["webdevcody","sphaerophoria","codewithantonio","dotnet","javascriptmastery"],"similar":[{"id":"smashing","handle":"smashing","name":"Smashing Magazine","is_squad":false,"x":-1.5728,"y":3.7627,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":530,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/smashing","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":1.199823,"median_upvotes":1.0,"author_present_share":0.060377,"hype_score":0.00566,"avg_read_time":13.130769,"tag_diversity":0.413208},"top_tags_preview":[["ux",153],["webdev",144],["css",85]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[3.7206,-1.5147],"cadence_depth":[8.8824,7.6176],"hype_variety":[-0.9559,8.1618],"title_style":[-5.0294,-0.1912]}},{"id